# 🐧 Linux

## Cron Jobs

Cron is a Linux scheduling service used to automatically execute tasks at specified times.

Examples:

* Daily backups
* Log cleanup
* Running maintenance scripts
* Scheduled system tasks

---

## Command

```bash
crontab -e
```

Purpose:

Edit the current user's scheduled Cron Jobs.

---

## Example

```text
0 2 * * * backup.sh
```

Meaning:

Run the backup script every day at 2:00 AM.

---

## Why Cron Jobs Are Useful

* Automates repetitive tasks
* Reduces manual work
* Ensures regular system maintenance
* Improves system reliability

---

# 🌐 Networking

## VLAN (Virtual Local Area Network)

A VLAN logically divides one physical network into multiple separate networks.

Example:

One office switch:

* Finance VLAN
* HR VLAN
* IT VLAN

Although all devices are connected to the same physical switch, VLANs separate network traffic between departments.

---

## Benefits of VLANs

* Better network security
* Reduced broadcast traffic
* Easier network management
* Department isolation
* Improved network performance

